BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 433.00 Td (gold and predicted answers, handles scaled units such as thousands and millions, and compares) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 420.00 Td (values with an absolute tolerance of 0.1 and a relative tolerance of 0.01. This is important) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 407.00 Td (because statistical answers are often expressed with different wording while containing the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 394.00 Td (value. The evaluator also handles KNBS table unit markers such as `\('000\)`, where table values) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 381.00 Td (must be interpreted in thousands.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 365.00 Td (For text-heavy rows, the evaluator also records fuzzy text similarity, token-overlap F1, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 352.00 Td (semantic similarity. These are useful diagnostics, but numeric rows are primarily judged by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 339.00 Td (exact or numeric match because most benchmark questions ask for statistical values. This is why) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 326.00 Td (exact match can be low while overall accuracy is high: the model may answer "inflation was 6.3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 313.00 Td (per cent" while the gold cell contains only "6.3".) Tj ET
